+| I-27 | The skill's self-verify procedure runs the build, a first-step render check, and a browser visual composition check, and it uses the full `npm run verify` before completion. Visual checks cover the first, last, and dense or key steps, plus a narrow viewport when responsive-sensitive. It prefers the project-local screenshot helper, or writes any ad hoc Playwright helper only under the project root. It fixes failures and re-checks instead of reporting success, reviews the helper's warnings, fixes accidental collisions and chrome polish, and marks only genuine intentional overlaps with the allow-overlap marker. | specs/presentation-skill: Self-verify before reporting completion, Generated presentation quality bar; design.md Skill step 4 | AT-001, AT-002, AT-004 | both (reviewer R-23, R-24) | SKILL.md phase 4; `scripts/inspect-presentation.mjs` | skill.test.ts; AT-001/002/004 journeys executed including repair of a build failure, a runtime console error, accidental overlap, indistinct nav and attribution, and marking only the genuine overlap (acceptance-evidence.md). Pass with the same-agent caveat. | done |
+| I-28 | The project passes `npm ci`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build`, and `npm run verify`, with `playwright` as a devDependency and `test`, `lint`, `verify`, and `inspect` scripts defined. No CI configuration (such as `.github/workflows/`) is added. | CLAUDE.md; design.md Migration Plan; proposal.md | Run the full suite; check that no workflow files exist | implementor | `package.json` | Ran `npm ci`, `npm test` (66 pass), `npm run lint`, `npm run build`, `npm run verify` (PASS), `npm run test:integration` (17 pass). No `.github/`. Pass. | done |
+| I-29 | Terminology is consistent: "presentation" is the canonical term across the skill, kit, and docs. "Talk" appears only as the `Talk.tsx` filename. | proposal.md Technical Approach | grep review of SKILL.md, kit, and templates | implementor | SKILL.md, kit, templates | tests/unit/skill.test.ts checks "talk" only as synonym/Talk.tsx; grep of kit/templates. Pass. | done |
+| I-30 | Unit and contract tests cover the isolated logic: scene-state and step numbering, nav clamping and keys, fit scaling, the registry, and sample outline validation. The integration (INT-001, INT-002), end-to-end (E2E-001, E2E-002), and agent acceptance (AT-001 to AT-004) layers run on throwaway copies and leave the source repo unchanged. AT-003 uses `chrome-devtools-axi`; disposable projects and preview processes are cleaned up afterward. | test-plan.md Coverage Strategy, Coverage Map | `npm test`, plus the integration and E2E suites; acceptance evidence | both (reviewer R-30) | `tests/unit/**`, `tests/integration/**` | Unit/contract (80), INT-001/002, E2E-001/002 pass; AT-003 via AXI; AT-001, AT-002, AT-004 executed in disposable projects with evidence in `acceptance-evidence.md` (the implementing agent played both user and agent, not an independent interviewer). Pass with that caveat. | done |
+| I-31 | The skill is a distributable hybrid package: an agent procedure (SKILL.md), reusable templates, and the shared scene kit combine so that a browser presentation can be created from a topic. | proposal.md What Changes; design.md Skill, Repository layout | Inspect `skills/presentation/` package contents; AT-001 and AT-002 exercise the public workflow | reviewer (R-1) | `skills/presentation/` (SKILL.md, scripts, templates) + kit | skill.test.ts; the distributable package (SKILL.md, scaffold.mjs, templates) exercised end to end by AT-001/002/004 and the bootstrap/scaffold tests. Pass. | done |
+| I-32 | Primitives and chrome expose stable identity, class, data, and style hooks. Authors can place literal per-step coordinates and use raw motion elements with stable `layoutId`s, and none of this adds kit-owned visual styling. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations: Style ownership boundary (Kit primitives expose style hooks, Coordinate-heavy diagrams); design.md Generic node primitives | Contract tests plus a styled fixture showing hooks, coordinate placement, and raw-motion interoperability | reviewer (R-14) | `src/presentation-kit/nodes/*` | tests/unit/kit-contract.test.tsx: id/class/data/style passthrough, `at` coordinates, Appear/raw interop, no fallback colors. Pass. | done |
